  "title": "Fujiya Hotel",
  "cell": "xn/xn6",
  "geometryBasis": "Six named native building footprints within the hotel’s main parcel locate the surviving historic and newer structures. Unflattened national GSI DEM5A relief positions the different foundation datums on the slope.",
  "sectionBasis": "The exact Kusakabe photograph on Qualla and the Rijksmuseum’s separate 1891–1900 albumen print show the Main’s twin faceted bays, temple-like tile roof, deep cornice and veranda. The standing hotel’s architecture guide and renovation account describe the other mapped wings and their period-specific roofs.",
  "limitations": [
    "Six principal buildings are modeled in the main compound. The detached Kikka-so across the road, shops, interior fittings and small garden structures are outside scope.",
    "Facade and roof profiles draw from the named current buildings, historic records and the hotel’s restoration descriptions. Later wing heights, balcony sequences, exact trim shades and small windows are approximate.",
    "The discrete building datums follow the national elevation survey. Retaining walls, courtyard steps and interpolated ground beneath the buildings are approximations."
